; The transactions of xact-price-inference-hours.test with their postings
; swapped.  The first posting's commodity is the one bought, whichever side
; that is, so here the dollars and euros are bought at 24s each: the income
; postings take the lots, the price history gains $ and € in seconds, and
; -V values the income in hours.
;
; This case never depended on the order of the balance's map: the
; currencies are not reduced, so the posting's commodity was always found.
; It pins the other half of the rule, which preferring the reduced unit, or
; the first commodity in sorted order (s before €), would break.

2024/01/05 Acme
    Income:Acme               $-1500
    Assets:Billable              10h

2024/01/20 Globex
    Income:Globex              €-300
    Assets:Billable               2h

test reg --lots
24-Jan-05 Acme                  Income:Acme            $-1500 {24s} [2024/01/05] $-1500 {24s} [2024/01/05]
                                Assets:Billable              10.00h $-1500 {24s} [2024/01/05]
                                                                          10.00h
24-Jan-20 Globex                Income:Globex          €-300 {24s} [2024/01/20] $-1500 {24s} [2024/01/05]
                                                                          10.00h
                                                        €-300 {24s} [2024/01/20]
                                Assets:Billable               2.00h $-1500 {24s} [2024/01/05]
                                                                          12.00h
                                                        €-300 {24s} [2024/01/20]
end test

test prices --now 2024/12/31
2024/01/05 $                 24s
2024/01/20 €                 24s
end test

test bal -V --now 2024/12/31
              12.00h  Assets:Billable
             -12.00h  Income
             -10.00h    Acme
              -2.00h    Globex
--------------------
                   0
end test
